{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And I declared, etc.</b> The meaning is: after I declared to you the future things, so that you would not say when they come to pass — your idols, which you used to worship in your land, made them, and they commanded and they were." "The meaning of <b>them</b> is like the way of the Name [i.e., the object suffix, as elsewhere]."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {0 "Reading עשום as עֲשׂוּם, 'they made'; the unpointed form could also be read as 'you made them,' but the parallel clause 'they commanded and they were' requires the idols as subject."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:31.631675991Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}